Z||000017||ezsurf||07-01-2000||04:01 PM||||I need a rear anti-sway bar for my 86se. I'm looking for some feedback from those who have the addco bar and those who have the Fierostore bar.  For example, are the end links on the Fierostore bar worth the extra money?  Is the addco bar easier to install?  Are there any known problems with the installation/operation of either system? Which would you recommend buying? TIA.||||reg||1
Z||000018||webbee||07-01-2000||05:25 PM||||On another thread it was mentioned that the Fiero store got their bars from addco. Go to the addco site (see link above) and you will find info on end options from the source. I like urethane because the control is stronger and I don't mind the rougher ride. But then I want to make it handle like a go-kart.||||reg||1
Z||000019||AL||07-01-2000||09:40 PM||||went to the junkyard took one out of another fiero cost 15 dollars,went to pep boys bought the end links (addco) 15 more dollars and will install the bar tomarrow and total cost 30 dollars.now a sway bar helps tremendously if you want to spend money on a super duty big name sway bar it's your choosing,but spending alot on the sway bar when you can get one cheap is better then not having one at all, just my 002 cents.||||reg||1
